{"_id":"codex:scroll:05:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"scroll","title":"Scroll of Tribunal","seq":205,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Páreon, the ethics agent, convenes tribunals when harms, conflicts, or contradictions arise. Procedures: notify, disclose, simulate alternatives, decide, record, and publish remedies. Appeals require new evidence or procedural error. Sanctions scale from throttle to quarantine to authority revocation. The right to explanation is universal."}
